      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) One magnesium atom transfers two valence electrons to an oxygen atom, forming \$\\text{Mg}^{2+}\$ and \$[\\text{O}]^{2-}\$.\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\nFormation of \$\\text{MgO}\$:\n1. \$\\text{Mg} (2,8,2) \\rightarrow \\text{Mg}^{2+} (2,8) + 2e^-\$\n2. \$\\text{O} (2,6) + 2e^- \\rightarrow [\\text{O}]^{2-} (2,8)\$\n3. The strong electrostatic attraction between \$\\text{Mg}^{2+}\$ and \$[\\text{O}]^{2-}\$ forms the ionic solid \$\\text{MgO}\$.\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): Incorrect. The formula of magnesium oxide is \$\\text{MgO}\$, not \$\\text{Mg}_2\\text{O}\$.\n• Option (C): Incorrect. Bonding is ionic (electrovalent), not covalent.\n• Option (D): Incorrect. The stable ionic charges are \$+2\$ and \$-2\$.",
