      ],
      stepByStepSolution: "Correct Answer: (A) Applying a coating of zinc (or using Teflon/seasoned oil)\n\nScientific Principle / Key Concept:\nAlthough applying grease and paint are standard rust prevention methods for iron tools and gates, they cannot be used on an iron frying pan because:\n1. Grease will contaminate cooking food.\n2. Paint will scorch, melt, and peel off when heated on a stove, emitting noxious fumes.\nHence, a protective metallic zinc coating (or seasoning/Teflon coating) is the appropriate choice among standard metallurgical options presented in the NCERT exercise.\n\nDetailed Distractor & Misconception Analysis:\n• Option (B): Incorrect. Grease ruins cooking.\n• Option (C): Incorrect. Paint burns at stove temperatures.\n• Option (D): Incorrect. 'All of the above' ignores the cooking context.",
